 137	    T2["generation byte-identical across runs<br/>and input order, tests/contract.rs:93"]
 138	    NM["codebase name: --name, else the<br/>checkout directory's name<br/>main.rs:159-161"]
 139	    O --> BY
 140	    P --> BY
 141	    H --> BY
 142	    A --> BY
 143	    PO --> BY
 144	    BY --> T1
 145	    BY --> T2
 146	    NM -.->|leaks into output| BY
 147	```
 148	
 149	**What it shows.** Five mechanisms feed the guarantee and two tests hold it;
 150	one input, the codebase name, comes from outside the source bytes unless it is
 151	pinned.
 152	
 153	**Why it is this way.** The model crate states the four-clause contract that
 154	downstream crates rely on (`crates/sealmap-model/src/lib.rs:18`-`34`). CI pins
 155	`--name sealmap` so the checkout directory cannot leak into the corpus, as the
 156	rename commit records (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:25`).
 157	
 158	**Tension (determinism contract vs CLI):** "no ambient data"
 159	(`crates/sealmap-model/src/lib.rs:33`-`34`) holds for the model's types, but the
 160	CLI names the codebase after the canonicalised checkout directory when no
 161	name is given (`crates/sealmap/src/main.rs:177`-`182`), and that name reaches
 162	the index and overview, so two clones in differently named directories
 163	produce different bytes.
